{"id": "EUVD-2026-103656", "enisaUuid": "f59cdaf5-3255-3d03-977e-7e4cdc6572c4", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nbpf: Check params size before reading reserved fields\n\nbpf_crypto_ctx_create() is a kfunc whose second argument is declared\nwith the __sz annotation, so the verifier only guarantees that\nparams__sz bytes of params are valid.  The function nevertheless reads\nparams->reserved[0] and params->reserved[1] (offsets 14 and 15) before\ncomparing params__sz against the size of struct bpf_crypto_params, so a\nBPF program can pass a shorter buffer and have the kernel read past the\nregion that was validated for it.\n\nMove the size check in front of the reserved field reads.", "datePublished": "2026-10-18T15:19:26", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:22:38", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/e03253f5d65ebcd2a6d479f140c3bd9c7e4fb84a", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/cd12d3e08620257fbcaa262785d7f4b9473afc7a", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/86a0e945fb645ea90233fde239cd2de79f01974c", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/a11212910cf09b2fe8db9afa41ef60c4f81879c5"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-98611", "GHSA-3j3q-mxmx-xwq4"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.17, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "26186272-53d8-3c5f-a71c-cba9df7cd12c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "3e1c6f35409f9e447bf37f64840f5b65576bfb78 <cd12d3e08620257fbcaa262785d7f4b9473afc7a"}, {"id": "459fa17b-8309-38cb-bec1-97be0ff90112", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.9"}, {"id": "50c85990-5d52-39db-8096-2e4e8ae7acf1", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.10"}, {"id": "5ac364f8-7ab7-336d-a680-55595336458e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "8c34fc38-4782-366f-aa1f-0361374750eb", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "91cab5ba-a350-33ba-b045-7e8d05cdd9fa", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "3e1c6f35409f9e447bf37f64840f5b65576bfb78 <86a0e945fb645ea90233fde239cd2de79f01974c"}, {"id": "9f665485-0455-38ea-9c50-981a3e234173", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "3e1c6f35409f9e447bf37f64840f5b65576bfb78 <e03253f5d65ebcd2a6d479f140c3bd9c7e4fb84a"}, {"id": "a1571045-1117-3b09-8d76-8ba8f14cdd91", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.55"}, {"id": "b2258ad9-208a-3f52-85fb-378530e424fc", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "3e1c6f35409f9e447bf37f64840f5b65576bfb78 <a11212910cf09b2fe8db9afa41ef60c4f81879c5"}, {"id": "ed471f34-808d-3ed7-9dae-c67294d967fa", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.112"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "7c40bb00-65b6-3af3-b9f7-8b62e8127baf", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}